By Pythagoras, $\angle ABC = 90^\circ$.  Let $P$ and $Q$ be the projections of $D$ onto $BC$ and $AB$, respectively.

[asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, P, Q;

A = (0,3);
B = (0,0);
C = (4,0);
D = (12/7,12/7);
P = (12/7,0);
Q = (0,12/7);

draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(B--D);
draw(P--D--Q);

label("$A$", A, NW);
label("$B$", B, SW);
label("$C$", C, SE);
label("$D$", D, NE);
label("$P$", P, S);
label("$Q$", Q, W);
