We have $\tan R = \frac{PQ}{PR}$ and $\sin R = \frac{PQ}{RQ} = \frac{PQ}{20}$, so $\tan R = 4\sin R$ gives us $\frac{PQ}{PR} = 4\cdot \frac{PQ}{20} = \frac{PQ}{5}$.  From $\frac{PQ}{PR} = \frac{PQ}{5}$, we have $PR = \boxed{5}$.

question:
Let \[f(n) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
n^2-2 & \text{ if }n<0, \\
2n-20 & \text{ if }n \geq 0.
\end{array}
\right.\]What is the positive difference between the two values of $a$ that satisfy the equation $f(-2)+f(2)+f(a)=0$?

